# W3+W4 done — cadence containers built, consumers adopted, every adoption deletes what it replaced

**Note on inputs:** the consensus report file the prompt names (`collab/1789842300000-architect-dao-stream-waitset-consensus-report.md`) does not exist in this worktree or anywhere in its git history — I built from the plan verbatim (its *Revision — 2026-09-20 consensus reconciliation* section records the closed disputes, items 4/5/9 covering everything the prompt cites).

## W3 — what was built

**`src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset/cadence.cljc`** (pure, requires nothing): `init` (validates `{:poll-ms … :backoff {:factor :ceiling-ms …}}` at composition time) and `(cadence-step cadence-state moved?) → {:cadence-state … :sleep-ms …}`. Semantics: an idle round arms the current interval and climbs the curve; a moved round resets fully to `:poll-ms` (no pre-climb); the ceiling caps both directions. Never calls `check`, reads no clock, touches no stream — tested on all hosts with no fixture.

**Three host drivers, one namespace `dao.stream.waitset.driver`, each docstring-labelled *host policy*, holding zero interpreter state:**
- **clj** (`make-wake`/`nudge!`/`sleep!`): a `LinkedBlockingQueue` of contentless Booleans; `sleep!` polls with the timeout and drains surplus, so nudges coalesce into one wake. *select* with the wakeup pipe.
- **cljs / cljd** (`make-wake tick`/`arm!`/`disarm!`/`nudge!`): exactly one timer, cancel-and-rearm (Node timers unref'ed); firing calls the composition root's own zero-arg tick; `nudge!` cancels and schedules the tick once on a microtask, with a pending flag that stays up *through* the tick (cleared in a `finally` after it), so repeated nudges coalesce and an in-tick nudge is swallowed — never re-enters.

No `make-driver` container, no atom holding a waitset, no `:budget`, no external parks, no `run-loop!`.

